James inquired about linker errors related to function templates `streamInsertVector` and `streamExtractVector` defined in `SerializationTools.cpp` but declared in `SerializationTools.h`. The issue arose because function templates must generally be defined in the header file for compilation units that use them to instantiate specific types. I recommended moving the definitions directly into the header or using explicit instantiations in the `.cpp` file. Additionally, I pointed out issues in the implementation, including incorrect vector iteration and usage of `insert` instead of `push_back`. This digest summarizes the technical advice provided to resolve the linking errors effectively.
